    "narrative": "The offensive engine for the Austin Waves today is undoubtedly **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), who headlines our lineup against Ober. His elite efficiency is bolstered by a favorable 4.78 xERA matchup and a secondary bump from Ober\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a high-leverage opportunity for **Gunnar Henderson** to exploit the basepaths. Joining him in the elite tier are **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.82) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (76.18). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a strong platoon advantage against the lefty Sandoval, while **Luis Robert Jr.** benefits from a similar dynamic platoon edge against P\u00e9rez. We are also looking for high-ceiling performances from **Kyle Tucker** (71.02) and **Jacob Wilson** (72.73), both of whom are positioned to take advantage of favorable pitching environments to keep our scoring volume high across the board.\n\nThe bench decision process was tight today, with **Nasim Nunez** (48.11) emerging as the most difficult omission. While **Nasim Nunez** offers valuable speed, he was ultimately benched due to a tougher matchup against the lefty Imanaga and a lower projected efficiency compared to the starters in our OF and MI slots. Meanwhile, we are exercising caution regarding the 31% rain risk affecting the game featuring **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos**; while both remain in the starting lineup, their efficiency scores are moderately sensitive to these conditions. We are monitoring **Liam Hicks** and **Andy Pages** closely, as both rely on projected lineup spots; should they drop lower in the order than anticipated, their scores will regress accordingly. The team is positioned to maximize our 5x5 categories, provided the weather holds in the contests featuring our key middle infielders.",
